id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-03-12T17:24:41Z","updated_at":"2025-04-05T19:25:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in godot 4.4\n\n### System information\n\ntested on Ubuntu 24.10  and Windows 10 - Intel Integrated Graphics 630 - Compatibility mode\n\n### Issue description\n\nSince version 4.4 (in 4.3 everything was fine) using the \"always\" update mode of a reflection probe does not update his reflections. When a game gets launched with this mode applied by default the reflection is black because it does not have the probe created by the \"once\" mode. In fact if \"once\" gets enabled and then you switch back to \"always\" the reflection appears but yet it does not update itself when it is moved. This issue occurs both in-game and in-editor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nJust create a project with a reflecting object, select always mode, start the game and the reflection is black. Try to move the object around to see that it does not get updated\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19214586/mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104041/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}